    <div>
      <h2 id="landmark-title">The Landmark for Peace</h2>
      <p>The Landmark for Peace is a memorial sculpture in Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Park, on the north side of Indianapolis. It honors Robert F. Kennedy and Martin Luther King Jr., and shows the two men reaching out toward each other.</p>
      <p>It was designed by Indiana artist Greg Perry, and the bronze portraits were created by Indianapolis sculptor Daniel Edwards. On April 4, 2018, the memorial was designated the Kennedy-King National Commemorative Site.</p>
      <p>After a rebuild of the park around it, the memorial has reopened with new exhibits and new walking paths. It's worth a visit.</p>
    </div>
